Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check used `b.url === inc.url`, an exact case-sensitive comparison, so `https://example.com/a` never matched `https://EXAMPLE.com/a`.

What changed:
- Added a `normalize()` helper that lowercases URLs (via `new URL(url).href` when parseable, falling back to plain lowercasing for non-URLs), and compared on that instead of the raw strings.

Verified:
- Case-differing URL now merges into a single entry with unioned tags (`["x","y"]`); distinct URLs still append.
- `deno test` passes (3 passed, 0 failed); lint clean.

Left: no dedicated test in the repo covers this path — worth adding one if you want regression protection.


